Phase 3 recorded evidence (2026-07-19):

- All 11 named files were renamed to `*_spec.lua` and converted directly to
  `describe()`, `it()`, and Luassert. Static searches of all native specs found
  no active `luaunit`, `native_tests`, or `add_test` references.
- Conversion reconciliation found 190 baseline assertions and 190 native
  assertions, plus 54 baseline static case registrations and 54 native static
  registrations. The generated matrices expand the batch to 79 runtime cases.
- All four approximate comparisons use `assert.near` with the former LuaUnit
  double-precision default epsilon supplied explicitly as `2^-52`.
- Each spec was run directly. Ten specs passed cleanly. `search_spec.lua` ran
  21 cases with 17 successes and exactly the four accepted failures:
  `ranking: earlier selected filter receives priority bonus`,
  `ranking: full and partial matches remain in results`,
  `ranking: mixed stat kinds evaluate together`, and
  `ranking: raw score breaks an exact weighted-score tie`.
- The complete current Busted suite ran 169 tests and reported
  `165 successes / 4 failures / 0 errors / 0 pending`. No production or runner
  file changed, and no other case failed.
- Independent regression validation passed: Lua 5.4.6 parsed 66 production
  files and 64 test/support files, the package-tool contract suite returned 0,
  and `git diff --check` reported no errors.
- The Phase 0 manifest reconciles to exactly 30 native specs: the 19 Phase 2
  specs plus these 11. The 27 remaining `*_test.lua` files belong to Phases 4
  and 5.
- Per-spec runtime totals are: `active_unit_provider` 2;
  `candidate_provider` 2; `candidate_filter_family_provider` 3;
  `race_filter_provider` 5; `attribute_descriptions` 2; `attributes` 27;
  `residents` 9; `unit_scope_filter_provider` 1; `search_session` 5;
  `search` 21; and `candidate_pipeline_characterization` 2.
